# Data layer

- Schema changes update three places together: the Drizzle tables in `packages/schemas`, the Supabase migration in `infra/supabase`, and the PowerSync sync rules in `infra/powersync`.
- Ids are UUIDv7. Rows have `updated_at` and `deleted_at`. Conflicts are last-write-wins.
- The app boots PowerSync without `connect()`. Cloud sync connects only after the user opts in.
- Never put the AI provider key, Supabase key, or PowerSync URL into a synced table. Those live in secure storage.
- Repositories hide SQL. Screens do not import the database client.
